#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:2
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Ship Yard"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:10
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"A ship yard is where starships are built, maintained and enhanced. They "
"typically get built in to stations to facilitate services such as energy "
"recharging, hull repair, probe and ordnance replenishment, etc. This section "
"of the science database shows ship types that might get upgraded by ship "
"yards in the area and the details around potentially available upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:22
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"The MP52 Hornet is a significantly upgraded version of MU52 Hornet, with "
"nearly twice the hull strength, nearly three times the shielding, better "
"acceleration, impulse boosters, and a second laser cannon."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:30
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"The ZX model is an improvement on the WX-Lindworm with stronger hull and "
"shields, faster impulse and tubes, more missiles and a single weak, turreted "
"beam. The 'Worm' as it's often called, is a bomber-class starfighter. While "
"one of the least-shielded starfighters in active duty, the Worm's launchers "
"can pack quite a punch. Its goal is to fly in, destroy its target, and fly "
"out or be destroyed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:38
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Player variant of the Phobos M3. Not as strong as the Atlantis, but has "
"front firing tubes, making it an easier to use ship in some scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:46
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Long range narrow beam and some point defense beams, broadside missiles. "
"Agile for a frigate"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:54
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"This combat-specialized Piranha F12 adds mine-laying tubes, combat "
"maneuvering systems, and a jump drive."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:62
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Popular among traders and smugglers, the Flavia is a small cargo and "
"passenger transport. It's cheaper than a freighter for small loads and short "
"distances, and is often used to carry high-value cargo discreetly.\n"
"\n"
"The Flavia Falcon is a Flavia transport modified for faster flight, and adds "
"rear-mounted lasers to keep enemies off its back.\n"
"\n"
"The Flavia P.Falcon has a nuclear-capable rear-facing weapon tube and a warp "
"drive."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:70
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"A Flavia P. Falcon with better hull and shields, a jump drive, two turreted "
"beams covering both sides and a forward and rear tube. The nukes and mines "
"are gone"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:78
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"A refitted Atlantis X23 for more general tasks. The large shield system has "
"been replaced with an advanced combat maneuvering system and improved "
"impulse engines. Its missile loadout is also more diverse. Mistaking the "
"modified Atlantis for an Atlantis X23 would be a deadly mistake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:86
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"A number of missile tubes range around this ship. Beams were deemed lower "
"priority, though they are still present. Stronger defenses than a frigate, "
"but not as strong as the Atlantis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:94
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"A number of beams bristle from various points on this gunner. Missiles were "
"deemed lower priority, though they are still present. Stronger defenses than "
"a frigate, but not as strong as the Atlantis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:102
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Benedict is an improved version of the Jump Carrier"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:110
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"Kiriya is Warp Carrier based on the jump carrier with stronger shields and "
"hull and with minimal armament"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:118
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"A fairly standard cruiser. Stronger than average beams, weaker than average "
"shields, farther than average jump drive range"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:126
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"It's all about the missiles for this model. Broadside tubes shoot homing "
"missiles (30!), front, homing, EMP and nuke. Comparatively weak shields, "
"especially in the rear. Sluggish impulse drive."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:134
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"The Ender battle station is a huge ship with many defensive features. It can "
"be docked by smaller ships."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:142
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid "Small mine laying vessel with minimal armament, shields and hull."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:150
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"The Striker is the predecessor to the advanced striker, slow but agile, but "
"does not do an extreme amount of damage, and lacks in shields."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/player_ship_upgrade_downgrade_path_scenario_utility.lua:158
msgctxt "scienceDB"
msgid ""
"One of the first and smallest starfighters ever manufactured. It's a "
"favorite for collectors now. Strong beams, though they are mounted "
"awkwardly. A bit slower than modern starfighters. Stronger hull and shields "
"than today's Hornet."
msgstr ""

